From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pkgdemon <pkgdemonteam@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 13:32:49 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] NextBSD: bcm2835_fbd hands the Pi's firmware framebuffer to
 the boot splash

The Raspberry Pi 5 boots with no loader and no UEFI: the firmware loads
kernel8.img directly, so at cninit the NextBSD platform expert has no
boot video record and no EFI framebuffer and falls back to text.  The
firmware framebuffer appears only when bcm2835_fbd(4) attaches
(patches 0027, 0033, 0034).

Hand it to the platform expert first, with PE_late_console_fb(): when
cninit's half of the decision was graphics (no -v, -s, -a, no serial
console requested) and nothing has claimed the console, it becomes
PE_state.video and the console enters kPEGraphicsMode, the way xnu's
ARM platform expert takes the video record from the device tree.
vt(4)'s vd_init on it then paints the compiled-in splash and starts the
spinner instead of blanking (patch 0095), and the splash lasts until
getty's TIOCSCTTY as on amd64.

On -v, -s and serial-console boots the call is a no-op.

Part of nextbsd/nextbsd#542 (nextbsd-kernel#411).
---
 sys/arm/broadcom/bcm2835/bcm2835_fbd.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sys/arm/broadcom/bcm2835/bcm2835_fbd.c b/sys/arm/broadcom/bcm2835/bcm2835_fbd.c
index 9ad035f604434b357931ee0d25f8e8d40b3d5409..dfcb587fcea44f3a833c73146da6e7b788fa6cf1 100644
--- a/sys/arm/broadcom/bcm2835/bcm2835_fbd.c
+++ b/sys/arm/broadcom/bcm2835/bcm2835_fbd.c
@@ -39,6 +39,7 @@
 #include <sys/kernel.h>
 #include <sys/malloc.h>
 #include <sys/module.h>
+#include <sys/pexpert.h>
 
 #include <vm/vm.h>
 #include <vm/pmap.h>
@@ -252,6 +253,15 @@ bcm_fb_setup_fbd(struct bcmsc_softc *sc)
 		}
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * NextBSD (E19): the Pi 5 boots with no loader, so this firmware
+	 * framebuffer is the first the platform expert hears of.  On a
+	 * graphics boot it becomes the boot console here, and vt(4)'s
+	 * vd_init on it paints the compiled-in splash instead of a blank.
+	 * A no-op on -v, -s and serial-console boots.
+	 */
+	PE_late_console_fb(&sc->info);
+
 	fbd = device_add_child(sc->dev, "fbd", device_get_unit(sc->dev));
 	if (fbd == NULL) {
 		device_printf(sc->dev, "Failed to add fbd child\n");
